  "reason": "RNA single-profile PCA is the strongest completed result (acc 0.485, F1 0.464), while image ResNet is weak (acc 0.208, F1 0.172). The key uncertainty is whether the RNA signal can be improved by using multiple profiles with a simple aggregation before adding more complex encoders or fusion. config_002 keeps the same RNA encoder and modality as config_001 and tests the minimal multiprofile setting with avgpool, establishing a multiprofile PCA baseline and clarifying whether profile aggregation helps. This is a focused, high-information exploitation of the promising RNA direction under a limited budget."
